question.en:
Consider a project with the following `package.json` snippet for `husky` and `lint-staged`: 
```json
"husky": {
  "hooks": {
    "pre-commit": "lint-staged"
  }
},
"lint-staged": {
  "*.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}": [
    "eslint --fix",
    "prettier --write",
    "git add"
  ]
}
```
A developer commits a file `src/app.js` with both linting and formatting issues. What will be the *final* state of the staged file `src/app.js` after the `pre-commit` hook successfully completes?

